40. First Concrete Implementation

The first vertical slice should be deliberately small.

Phase 1

Build:

MOS MCP Client

Connect to:

Local MCP server

using:

stdio
Phase 2

Discover:

tools/list
resources/list
prompts/list

and register their metadata.

Phase 3

Put capability metadata into:

PostgreSQL

and hot discovery data into:

Redis
Phase 4

Execute one harmless tool:

system.info
Phase 5

Create:

cognition.operation

for the execution.

Phase 6

Store:

tool input
tool output
result hash
timing
MCP server
capability
agent
Phase 7

Project:

Agent
  ↓
Operation
  ↓
MCP Tool
  ↓
MCP Server

into TerminusDB.

Phase 8

Cache the result in Redis.

Phase 9

Run the same request again.

The expected path becomes:

Agent
 ↓
Attention
 ↓
Redis
 ↓
cached capability/result
 ↓
NO unnecessary MCP call

That gives us our first measurable MOS performance improvement.

41. Specification Invariants

These should be treated as hard rules.

Invariant 1

MCP is not authoritative storage.

Invariant 2

Redis is not authoritative storage.

Invariant 3

Tool authorization belongs to MOS policy + underlying system security.

Invariant 4

Every meaningful tool operation is auditable.

Invariant 5

External observations do not automatically become knowledge.

Invariant 6

Tool results are not automatically facts.

Invariant 7

Side-effecting operations are never represented solely by cached results.

Invariant 8

Historical tool operations remain immutable.

Invariant 9

Learned strategies are versioned rather than overwritten.

Invariant 10

MOS remains operational if Redis or an MCP server disappears.

Invariant 11

MOS remains model agnostic.

Invariant 12

MCP protocol state must not become MOS persistent state.

